<http://digistrucmed.org/entity/Yes._a_ECG_morphology_suggestive_of_RVOT_or_fascicular_origin,_negative_family_history,_normal_12-lead_ECG,_and_echocardiogram._b_e.g._atrioventricular_conduction_abnormalities,_Q_waves,_broad_QRS_complex,_ST/T_waves_deviations,_abnormally_high_or_low_voltages._Ventricular_dysfunction/dilatation/hypertrophy/wall_thinning,_wall_motion_abnormalities,_multitopic_PVCs/NSVTs/increasing_ventricular_arrhythmia_(VA)_burden_with_exercise._c_e.g._Brugada_pattern,_long/short_QT,_polymorphic/bidirectional_VA_with_exercise._d_Diagnostic_test_to_exclude_CAD_according_to_patient_profile_and_symptoms._e_Consider_re-evaluation_in_case_of_new_symptoms_or_changes_in_patient_clinical_condition> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Yes. a ECG morphology suggestive of RVOT or fascicular origin, negative family history, normal 12-lead ECG, and echocardiogram. b e.g. atrioventricular conduction abnormalities, Q waves, broad QRS complex, ST/T waves deviations, abnormally high or low voltages. Ventricular dysfunction/dilatation/hypertrophy/wall thinning, wall motion abnormalities, multitopic PVCs/NSVTs/increasing ventricular arrhythmia (VA) burden with exercise. c e.g. Brugada pattern, long/short QT, polymorphic/bidirectional VA with exercise. d Diagnostic test to exclude CAD according to patient profile and symptoms. e Consider re-evaluation in case of new symptoms or changes in patient clinical condition" .
